  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41653570",
      "title": "IoC And DI",
      "lectureOrder": 158,
      "videoOrder": 157,
      "sourceHash": "f74f3fa351021e2cfe46ecb76a56824a9c224e5a57f607cc330bdf4d84981103",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.373,
          "end": 3.21,
          "en": "(bright music)",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.21,
          "end": 5.43,
          "en": "-: So before starting with the Spring concept, we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.43,
          "end": 7.86,
          "en": "to understand one concept, in fact two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.86,
          "end": 10.92,
          "en": "One is IoC and second is DI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.92,
          "end": 12.39,
          "en": "I know they're the short forms,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.39,
          "end": 15.72,
          "en": "but the full form for this is inversion of control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.72,
          "end": 17.55,
          "en": "and dependency injection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.55,
          "end": 19.26,
          "en": "Of course, these are two different concept,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.26,
          "end": 21.21,
          "en": "but they are related.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 21.21,
          "end": 22.95,
          "en": "Okay, let's talk about IoC here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 22.95,
          "end": 26.46,
          "en": "See, IoC stands for inversion of control, which simply means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.46,
          "end": 29.43,
          "en": "that you are inverting the control,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.43,
          "end": 32.04,
          "en": "but where, what control you're inverting?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 32.04,
          "end": 34.98,
          "en": "See, the thing is, as a programmer you have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 34.98,
          "end": 36.12,
          "en": "multiple roles, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 36.12,
          "end": 37.86,
          "en": "So when you write a code, you make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 37.86,
          "end": 40.05,
          "en": "that you create the object, you make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 40.05,
          "end": 43.08,
          "en": "that you control the flow of the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 43.08,
          "end": 44.76,
          "en": "Now you'll be saying what's wrong with that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 44.76,
          "end": 47.04,
          "en": "See, I'm okay with the flow of the application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 47.04,
          "end": 49.92,
          "en": "but I'm not okay with the object creation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 49.92,
          "end": 51.27,
          "en": "Now you'll be saying, Hey, you know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 51.27,
          "end": 53.1,
          "en": "in the entire Java from start,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 53.1,
          "end": 54.75,
          "en": "we are talking about object creation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 54.75,
          "end": 57.3,
          "en": "And the way you do that is with help of new keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 57.3,
          "end": 58.26,
          "en": "What's wrong with that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 58.26,
          "end": 61.44,
          "en": "See, the thing is object creation is easy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 61.44,
          "end": 63.36,
          "en": "Of course, you can simply use a new keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 63.36,
          "end": 64.56,
          "en": "You get the object, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 64.56,
          "end": 67.71,
          "en": "So if you have a class, let's say class, laptop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 67.71,
          "end": 69.18,
          "en": "and if you want to create object off it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 69.18,
          "end": 70.71000000000001,
          "en": "you simply say laptop OBJ",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 70.71000000000001,
          "end": 72.6,
          "en": "equals new laptop and you get the object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 72.6,
          "end": 75.42,
          "en": "But the thing is we create the object and it's so easy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 75.42,
          "end": 77.52,
          "en": "So it is your responsibility to create the object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 77.52,
          "end": 80.01,
          "en": "It is your responsibility to maintain the object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 80.01,
          "end": 82.23,
          "en": "and also to destroy the object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 82.23,
          "end": 86.78999999999999,
          "en": "Basically, as a programmer, you are controlling everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 86.78999999999999,
          "end": 88.32,
          "en": "and that's where the problem starts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 88.32,
          "end": 90.66,
          "en": "Because when you try to manage all these things,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 90.66,
          "end": 92.82,
          "en": "you are not focusing on the main thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 92.82,
          "end": 93.78,
          "en": "What's the main thing here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 93.78,
          "end": 95.7,
          "en": "The main thing is a business logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 95.7,
          "end": 97.535,
          "en": "Every application is different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 97.535,
          "end": 101.7,
          "en": "And what makes them different is this business logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 101.7,
          "end": 102.87,
          "en": "So as a programmer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 102.87,
          "end": 105.24000000000001,
          "en": "your focus should be on the business logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 105.24000000000001,
          "end": 107.4,
          "en": "not on the object creation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 107.4,
          "end": 110.94,
          "en": "So what you want here is you want someone else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 110.94,
          "end": 113.1,
          "en": "to control this object creation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 113.1,
          "end": 115.77000000000001,
          "en": "That means you are inverting a control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 115.77000000000001,
          "end": 116.78399999999999,
          "en": "Earlier, you had a control,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 116.78399999999999,
          "end": 119.43,
          "en": "now you're giving the control to someone else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 119.43,
          "end": 121.26,
          "en": "That is inversion of control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 121.26,
          "end": 123.48,
          "en": "So it's not just for the object, but also for the flow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 123.48,
          "end": 125.13,
          "en": "Okay. So that's inversion of control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 125.13,
          "end": 126.48,
          "en": "Now to achieve this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 126.48,
          "end": 129.72,
          "en": "in Spring we have something called IoC containers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 129.72,
          "end": 132.06,
          "en": "So basically Spring works with container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 132.06,
          "end": 134.19,
          "en": "Imagine this container as a box",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 134.19,
          "end": 135.81,
          "en": "where you get all the objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 135.81,
          "end": 138.18,
          "en": "Now, when I say, hey, you don't have to create the object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 138.18,
          "end": 140.91,
          "en": "I mean as a programmer, you don't have to create the object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 140.91,
          "end": 142.98,
          "en": "Someone else have to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 142.98,
          "end": 144.69,
          "en": "And that's your Spring framework.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 144.69,
          "end": 146.28,
          "en": "Spring will create objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 146.28,
          "end": 148.2,
          "en": "for you and where you will keep it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 148.2,
          "end": 150.969,
          "en": "So inside this container, which is the IoC container,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 150.969,
          "end": 153.99,
          "en": "you will be having your objects and who will create it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 153.99,
          "end": 155.19,
          "en": "It is your Spring framework.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 155.19,
          "end": 156.96,
          "en": "That is your Spring, IoC,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 156.96,
          "end": 159,
          "en": "and the container name is IoC container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 159,
          "end": 161.04,
          "en": "Now, that concept is basically a principle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 161.04,
          "end": 164.46,
          "en": "So IoC is a principle which you follow to achieve this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 164.46,
          "end": 166.8,
          "en": "but how exactly you will make it work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 166.8,
          "end": 169.584,
          "en": "And that's where we have to use a design pattern called a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 169.584,
          "end": 174.3,
          "en": "dependency injection where you have the objects there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 174.3,
          "end": 177,
          "en": "but someone has to inject them to your application, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 177,
          "end": 179.46,
          "en": "So let's say you want to create a laptop class, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 179.46,
          "end": 182.1,
          "en": "And this laptop is basically dependent on a CPU.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 182.1,
          "end": 183.99,
          "en": "Of course you cannot run a laptop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 183.99,
          "end": 186.81,
          "en": "or you cannot use a laptop without CPU.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 186.81,
          "end": 188.73,
          "en": "So basically imagine you have two different classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 188.73,
          "end": 191.07,
          "en": "We got laptop class, we got CPU class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 191.07,
          "end": 195.54,
          "en": "and now inside your laptop class you need a CPU object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 195.54,
          "end": 198.39,
          "en": "So basically both this objects are available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 198.39,
          "end": 200.34,
          "en": "inside the container, but how will you link them?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 200.34,
          "end": 204.551,
          "en": "How will you inject the CPU object inside the laptop?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 204.551,
          "end": 206.4,
          "en": "And that's where we have to use a concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 206.4,
          "end": 207.96,
          "en": "of dependency injection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 207.96,
          "end": 210.93,
          "en": "How we are going to do that in Spring? We'll see that later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 210.93,
          "end": 214.53,
          "en": "But using Spring is not just creating the object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 214.53,
          "end": 217.74,
          "en": "but also injecting that into your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 217.74,
          "end": 220.82999999999998,
          "en": "That is your dependency injection design pattern,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 220.82999999999998,
          "end": 224.25,
          "en": "which you use to implement the IoC principle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 224.25,
          "end": 225.083,
          "en": "Okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 225.083,
          "end": 225.916,
          "en": "Now, most of the time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 225.916,
          "end": 229.35,
          "en": "you might see people exchanging these two words",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 229.35,
          "end": 231.78,
          "en": "and that completely fine when it comes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 231.78,
          "end": 233.19,
          "en": "to building an application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 233.19,
          "end": 235.14,
          "en": "But behind the scenes things are bit different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 235.14,
          "end": 236.61,
          "en": "So IoC is a principle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 236.61,
          "end": 238.71,
          "en": "and dependency injection is a design pattern using which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 238.71,
          "end": 239.85,
          "en": "you can do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 239.85,
          "end": 243.21,
          "en": "So that's IoC and dependency injection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 243.21,
          "end": 245.07,
          "en": "And now we know when you talk about Spring,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 245.07,
          "end": 246.45,
          "en": "it has multiple projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 246.45,
          "end": 249.39,
          "en": "but one of the project deals with this concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 249.39,
          "end": 250.59,
          "en": "of dependency injection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 250.59,
          "end": 251.79,
          "en": "Now how do we implement that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 251.79,
          "end": 253.773,
          "en": "That, we'll see in the upcoming videos.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
